This is github Issue #337
by Marti2203.

dwarf_next_str_offsets_table() misreads every table after the first.


dwarfdump --print-str-offsets misreads a .debug_str_offsets section that holds more than one DWARF5 table, as any ld -r of two DWARF5 objects does:

Incorrect output:
 dwarfdump --print-str-offsets both.o
.debug_str_offsets
 table 0
 tableheader 0x00000000
 arrayoffset 0x00000000
 unit length 0x00000034
 entry size  4
 version     5
 padding     0x0
 arraysize   14
 Entry [   0]:  0x00000034 0x00000005 0x00000000 0x0000002d
 Entry [   4]:  0x00000031 0x000000a9 0x000000ab 0x000000ad
 Entry [   8]:  0x000000b1 0x000000b3 0x000000b8 0x000000ba
 Entry [  12]:  0x000000be 0x000000c3
 wasted      0 bytes

 table 1
 tableheader 0x00000040
 arrayoffset 0x00000040
 unit length 0x00000058
 entry size  4
 version     4

The bug suggests fixes to the code,
and these are all correct.
